    feat(hybrid): Andes V5 CSR transport -- mxstatus via X-macro (ABI v3), minimal

    This is the minimal step of the Andes V5 CSR transport, built up before the completion commit widens it. It advances the include/ submodule pin to ABI v3, which introduces struct hybrid_andes_csr and the HYBRID_ANDES_CSR_LIST X-macro as the single source of truth for the transported scalars. The QEMU plugin drains one scalar, mxstatus (the first entry of that list), and raises HYBRID_FLAG_ANDES when the gdbstub advertised the CSR, so the flag marks the block as live only on an Andes producer. The driver's state_diff gains the matching mxstatus verify row gated on FLAG_ANDES, and its unit test proves the row is compared under the flag and skipped without it. The remaining twelve Andes scalars, the PMA arrays, and the full X-macro drain loop every consumer iterates land in the completion commit.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

